{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}How It Works | ISDS Thematic Watcher{% endblock %}
{% block description %}The whole instrument on one chart, drawn deterministically from the repository it describes: the nine public sources, the automated pipeline, the AI research council, the researcher's verification column, and every Monday deliverable.{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<section class="page-head">
  <div class="measure">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol>
        <li><a href="{{ root }}index.html">Home</a></li>
        <li aria-current="page">How It Works</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>
    <p class="page-kicker">The instrument</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">How the instrument works</h1>
    <p class="page-lede">
      The whole system on one chart, drawn directly from the repository it
      describes &mdash; every box and arrow cites the file that implements it.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="measure">
    <div class="doc-body">
      <p>
        Read it top to bottom. The first band is the nine public sources checked
        on every run. Beneath it the work divides into four columns:
        <strong>the machine</strong> &mdash; the automated pipeline that collects,
        de-duplicates, scores, and quality-gates each candidate development;
        <strong>what gets sent</strong> &mdash; the emails and site updates each
        stage produces; <strong>the AI research council</strong> &mdash; the
        research agents, each box naming the model it runs on, that interpret the
        week under binding fact-verification gates; and <strong>Emory's
        verification column</strong> &mdash; no claim is published as fact without
        a human check against its original source. The moving dots trace work
        flowing through the system. On a desktop browser, hovering over any box
        shows its full description and the exact code behind it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figure class="workflow-figure">
    <div class="workflow-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Workflow chart; scrolls horizontally on small screens" tabindex="0">
      {{ workflow_svg | safe }}
    </div>
    <figcaption>
      Drawn deterministically from the repository's own workflow description; a
      build-time freshness check keeps it in step with the code it depicts.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>
{% endblock %}
